{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "fce7f304-c421-8b69-858f-27f193e66169",
  "created_at": "2026-02-22T10:13:01-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Wilson Pina",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Lorraine Medeiros",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:06:00-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Lorraine. We're on the storm line this morning, what can I help you with?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:06:07-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi. Yes. I am calling about the drain on our corner. Again."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:06:12-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Again, you said? Let me get the address first and I'll pull up what we have."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:06:18-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Eighteen Howard Street. In the Fifth Ward."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:06:21-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Eighteen Howard Street. And your name?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:06:24-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Wilson Pina. W-I-L-S-O-N. Pina, P-I-N-A."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:06:27-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Wilson Pina, P-I-N-A. Okay. And what's going on at the house?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:06:31-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The basement flooded. Last night, overnight Saturday into this morning. From the storm. This is the second time this winter."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:06:38-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Second time this winter. Okay. How much water are we talking?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:06:42-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "About five inches. Five. Last time it was two. So, you know. Better every time."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:06:48-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Five inches, and two the first time. And where's it getting in, do you know?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:06:54-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Same places. The window well on the street side, the glass there. And the basement windows. Exactly same as January. Nothing new. Just more."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:07:02-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Window well glass on the street side, and the basement windows. Same as before. Okay, I'm writing that down. And you think it's the drain at the corner?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:07:12-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I don't think. I know. I went out this morning, early. The catch basin at the corner, it's all buried in leaves. Completely. Covered. The water has nowhere to go, so it comes across the sidewalk, goes right to our window well. [line breaks up] ...like a river."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:07:28-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sorry, you cut out a little there. The basin's covered in leaves, and then what?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:07:34-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The water goes across, to our house. Like a river. Can you hear me now?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:07:40-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I've got you now, yup. Catch basin at the corner buried in leaves, water running across to the window well. Let me look at the history here. [pause] Okay. I see a call on this address January twelfth, that was a Monday. Nilson Pina?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:07:55-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "My father. Yes. He called after the first one. January tenth, the flood was. And the person said a crew will come look at the drain."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:08:04-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right, and I've got a note here that a crew went out Tuesday the thirteenth and cleared the grate, shoveled out silt around the basin."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:08:13-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "They cleaned the top. The grate. That's it. That's not looking at the drain. We were told somebody will look at the drain, what's wrong with it. Nobody looked. Nobody checked underneath, the pipe, anything. They sweep the top and leave. And now, look. Five inches."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:08:28-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Understood. So the grate got cleaned but nobody actually checked the line itself."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:08:33-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. That is what I am saying. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:08:37-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. What got wet down there this time, anything new?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:08:41-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No. Same things. File boxes, paperwork, my father keeps a lot. And the workbench, the hand tools. All wet again. We just dried them from last time. Nothing new is damaged. Just the same things, second time."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:08:54-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "File boxes of paperwork, the workbench and hand tools, same as before. Nothing new affected. Is the water still in there now?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:09:02-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Some. Going down slowly. We are pushing it out. [inaudible] ...the shop vac."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:09:07-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sorry, I lost the end of that."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:09:10-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I said we have the shop vac. We are handling inside. The inside is not your problem. The corner is your problem."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:09:18-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Fair enough. So here's what I'm going to do. I'm logging this as a repeat backup, same location, so it's flagged as the second time and not a brand new call."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:09:29-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. But I don't want only another crew to come sweep the leaves. I want somebody who knows. A supervisor. Or engineer. Somebody to look at the drain, really look. Why it backs up."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:09:41-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, a supervisor or an engineer to look at it. I can put in for a supervisor to call you back on that, and I'll note that you want the line looked at, not just the grate."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:09:54-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. Please write it like that. Not just the grate."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:09:58-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "'Not just the grate.' I'm typing it in your words. [pause] Okay. For the crew, with everything from the storm they're stretched today and tomorrow, but I can get this on the schedule for Tuesday, the twenty-fourth."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:10:11-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Tuesday. So two more days with leaves on top."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:10:15-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I know. If it rains again before then, call back and we'll bump it. And the supervisor callback, I'm putting that in for by Wednesday, the twenty-fifth."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:10:24-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "By Wednesday. Okay. Will they actually call? Last time we got promise also."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:10:29-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It's going in as a callback request with the repeat flag on it, so it goes to a supervisor directly, not the general list. What's the best number for you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:10:39-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "My cell. Four-oh-one, five-five-five, oh-one-five-nine."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:10:42-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Four-oh-one, five-five-five... was that oh-one-five-nine?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:10:44-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. Oh-one-five-nine."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:10:46-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, 401-555-0159. Best times?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:10:48-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Weekday is hard, I am with patients. But leave message, I call back at lunch. [clears] Sorry. Sorry, my voice."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:10:55-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem. You okay? You sound a little hoarse."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:10:59-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I am fine. I'm warming up. I sing in a community chorus, we have rehearsal this afternoon. So I do this in the car, humming. And instead I am standing in water at eight o'clock this morning."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:11:12-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Well, that's not the warm-up you wanted. Let me read it all back to you so you know what's in there."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:11:20-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. [line breaks up] ...go ahead."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:11:23-05:00",
      "duration": 39,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Eighteen Howard Street, Fifth Ward. Wilson Pina calling. Basement flooded a second time this winter, overnight Saturday into Sunday, about five inches. First flood was January tenth, about two inches, reported January twelfth by Nilson Pina. Water's coming in the same spots both times, the window well glass on the street side and the basement windows. Catch basin at the corner buried in leaves this morning. File boxes, workbench and hand tools wet again, nothing new. Crew on the thirteenth cleaned the grate only, line itself never checked. Crew booked Tuesday the twenty-fourth. Supervisor callback by Wednesday the twenty-fifth at 401-555-0159, leave a message, and you're asking for a supervisor or an engineer to look at the drain. Did I miss anything?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:12:02-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No. That's right. That's everything."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:12:04-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "And just so you know, if the leaves are piled on there again before Tuesday, you can rake them off the top if it's safe, but don't go reaching into the basin itself."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:12:15-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "We did already. This morning. My father and me. With the rake. Like a city crew, but free."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:12:22-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "[pause] Yeah, I hear you. I'll make sure that's in the notes too, that you cleared it yourselves this morning."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:12:29-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Fine. Do I get a number, for this? A reference?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:12:33-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It's attached to the address and your name, so if you call back, just give Eighteen Howard and anybody here can pull up the whole history, both floods."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:12:43-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Both floods. Good. Because I don't want to explain this again from the beginning."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:12:49-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You won't have to. It's all in there."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:12:52-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Thank you, Lorraine."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:12:54-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're welcome, Wilson. Good luck with the drying out, and with rehearsal."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-22T10:12:59-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thanks. Tuesday. [inaudible] ...bye."
    }
  ],
